<.shell current={:tabs}>
  <h1>Tabs</h1>
  <p class="lead">Pages about one record, a link each.</p>

  <div class="demo">
    <.tabs label="Member">
      <:tab navigate="#" current>Attendance</:tab>
      <:tab navigate="#">Qualifications</:tab>
      <:tab navigate="#">Groups</:tab>
      <:tab navigate="#">ID card</:tab>
      <:tab navigate="#">History</:tab>
    </.tabs>
  </div>

  <h3>Long labels</h3>
  <div class="demo">
    <.tabs label="Team settings">
      <:tab navigate="#">General</:tab>
      <:tab navigate="#">Team admins</:tab>
      <:tab navigate="#">Member logins</:tab>
      <:tab navigate="#" current>Hours tags for tax credit letters and the hours report</:tab>
      <:tab navigate="#">Chore categories</:tab>
      <:tab navigate="#">MCP tokens</:tab>
    </.tabs>
  </div>

  <h2>When to use</h2>
  <p>
    A few pages about the same record, such as a member's attendance, qualifications, and groups.
  </p>

  <h2>When not to use</h2>
  <p>
    To hide part of one page. Show it, or put it under <a href={page_path(:details)}>details</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>How it works</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Each tab is its own page with its own URL, so links and the back button work.</li>
    <li>
      Each tab is a grey tile. The tab for the page you are on is light blue with a bar at its
      foot.
    </li>
    <li>
      Tiles that don't fit wrap to the next row, at every width. A label too long for the screen
      wraps inside its tile, so the page never scrolls sideways.
    </li>
    <li>
      Tabs sit under the title, above both columns. An activity's are the exception: they sit in the main column under its
      map and description, Members · Equipment · History, so the activity stays on screen on every tab (decided 2026-10-28).
    </li>
    <li>Every page's tabs are the same height. There are no small tabs.</li>
    <li>
      Tabs share the <a href={page_path(:stat_switch)}>stat switch</a>'s look, since both switch
      what you're looking at. Their corners are square, unlike a <a href={page_path(:button)}>button</a>'s.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>In the app</h2>
  <p>
    <code>&lt;.tabs label="Member"&gt;</code>
    with a <code>&lt;:tab navigate=&#123;…&#125; current&gt;</code>
    for each page. <code>current</code>
    marks the page you are on.
  </p>
</.shell>
